<title>FRANCE: EU 96/97 subsidised grain exports almost tripled.</title>
<headline>EU 96/97 subsidised grain exports almost tripled.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union subsidised grain exports almost tripled in 1996/97 over the previous season, figures compiled by French grain office ONIC showed.</p>
<p>The forecast drawn from data supplied by EU-member states showed the European Union exported an estimated 26 million tonnes of grains and processed products with the aid of subsidies against 9.1 million in 1995/96.</p>
<p>Total grains and processed products exports reached 30.7 million tonnes against 22.1 million tonnes in 1995/96.</p>
<p>Details by cereals (in million tonnes)</p>
<p>SOFT WHEAT	   96/97	    95/96	 change</p>
<p>total exports	16.5	     12.7	  29 pct</p>
<p>of which grains     9.7		6.5	  49 pct</p>
<p>of which products   6.3		4.8	  30 pct</p>
<p>subsidies exports  13.6		3.0	 357 pct</p>
<p>BARLEY		  96/97	    95/96	change</p>
<p>Total exports	 9.1		4.0	 128 pct</p>
<p>of which grains     6.4		1.8	 261 pct</p>
<p>of which products   2.7		2.2	  21 pct</p>
<p>subsidised exports  9.1		3.2	 184 pct</p>
<p>MAIZE		   96/97	     95/96     Change</p>
<p>Total exports	 2.0		2.3	  -13 pct</p>
<p>of which grains     0.2		0.2	  -12 pct</p>
<p>of which products   1.8		1.9	   -8 pct</p>
<p>subsidised exports  1.2		1.2	    0 pct</p>
<p>TOTAL GRAIN	  96/97	    95/96	 Change</p>
<p>Total exports	30.7	     22.1	   39 pct</p>
<p>of which grains    18.1	     10.2	   77 pct</p>
<p>of which products  12.1	     10.2	   19 pct</p>
<p>subsidised exports 26.0		9.1	  185 pct</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
